## Error Patterns to Watch For

### 1. Async/Await Issues
```typescript
// ❌ Common mistake - not awaiting async operations
const handlePress = () => {
  someAsyncOperation(); // Missing await
};

// ✅ Correct
const handlePress = async () => {
  try {
    await someAsyncOperation();
  } catch (error) {
    handleError(error);
  }
};
```

### 2. Memory Leaks
```typescript
// ❌ Missing cleanup
useEffect(() => {
  const timer = setInterval(() => {}, 1000);
  // Missing cleanup
}, []);

// ✅ Proper cleanup
useEffect(() => {
  const timer = setInterval(() => {}, 1000);
  return () => clearInterval(timer);
}, []);
```

### 3. Type Safety Issues
```typescript
// ❌ Using any type
const data: any = await fetchData();

// ✅ Proper typing
const data: Article = await articlesService.getArticleById(id);
```

